The recent gcc-2.96-99 and gcc-2.96-101 compilers for alpha seem to be
broken: The sound blaster modules compiled with gcc-2.96-99 for EV6 crash
depmod (core dump). Fortunately, it works for targets EV56 and EV67.
Gcc-2.96-101 seems worse: it stops during linking the kernel with
drivers/char/char.o(.data+0x83a8): undefined reference to `local symbols in
discarded section .text.exit'
drivers/net/net.o(.data+0x260): undefined reference to `local symbols in
discarded section .text.exit'
both for EV6 and EV67 (I didn't try EV56 yet). Gcc-2.96-87 does not have
these problems, and neither do the x86 versions. Does anybody have made
similar experiences?

	Oliver




