Try making the root floppy from the images directory (on the CD) then
installing with

 >>> boot dka0 -fi /kernels/generic.gz -fl root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1

(the load_ramdisk=1 might be optional, can't remember).

For some reason the RedHat installer has issues on some machines....I
don't think anybody has ever tracked it down as the floppy has always been
an easy work around.

--rdp

