On Tue, Dec 04, 2001 at 02:27:50AM -0600, G.L. Grobe wrote:
> 
> I'm trying to install off the RH6.2 cd with the following command ...
> 
> >>> boot dka0 -fi /kernels/generic.gz -fl root=/dev/scd0
> 
> This finds the cd rom but results in ...
> ...
> Partition Check
> VFS: Cannot open root device 0b:00
> Kernel Panic VFS: Unable to mount root fs on 0b:00
                                                ^^^^

This is a device major 11 (in decimal), minor 0.  In another words
/dev/scd0.  Even if you are using a correct device to boot it
is very unlikely that you have a usable root file system on
/dev/scd0 hence this panic is a really correct, and expected, response.

IIRC a distribution CD for RH6.2 is already "smart" enough to know
what to do.  Try booting (assuming that dka0 is indeed correct for
your setup) with:
  
   boot dka0 -fl 0

If this does not work the load ramdisk (for example, make a floppy
from a ramdisk image you have on CD and append to your boot line
above "load_ramdisk=1").

  
> So I then tried ...
> 
> >>> boot dka0 -fi /kernels/generic.gz -fl root=/dev/hdc
> 
> and got pretty much the same results (only root device changed in the error
> above).

Sure.  Likewise.

  Michal




