On Wed, Dec 05, 2001 at 10:44:57AM -0500, Ghozlane Toumi wrote:
> 
> I just noticed that when building a 2.4.x kernels on a miata  (PWS 433au) , 
> the kernel uses the following optimisations flags  : "-mcpu=ev5 -Wa,-mev6"
> 
> Knowing that this box has an ev56 (/cpu/procinfo just confirmed this), 
> is there any reason why it doesn't use "-mcpu=ev56" ?

It should, dunno why it doesn't. Check the arch/alpha/Makefile.

> and uh.. well.. why the hell does it asks the assembler to build an ev6 
> binary ? i thought ev56 and ev5 where almost the same, but ev6 was another 
> generation ...

That switch (-Wa,-mev6) allows the assembler to process EV6 instructions.
This is necessary for "generic" kernels, in which there may be EV6 insns
explicitly included. It's not strictly needed for a MIATA kernel, but it
shouldn't hurt anything.

--Jay++

