As a slightly early Christmas present I purchased a Sony DVD drive for
my PWS500a. Whilst it works fine as a replacement for the CD drive I
can't seem to play DVDs. Using xine to play non-encrypted DVDs I get
"metronome errors" after playing one or two frames and xine just stops.
Using mpeg2dec it works fine but slowly (about 17 fps in a relatively
small window). What's depressing is if I mount the DVD and "export" it
via samba to my 500MHz celeron system running W2K I get much better
playback performance.

I understand that mpeg2dec has been hand optimised for Intel and I'm
sure a little bit of thought and work might get better performance but
am I really going to need to buy a hardware DVD decoder?? 

