I've got an SX164 running 2.4.16 and RH 7.1 with a D-Link 530TX (Via
Rhine II) Ethernet card.  I'm seeing lots of kernel unaligned accesses
whenever networking is enabled, but no user unaligned accesses.  Before
I start trying different kernels or different Ethernet cards, I'd like
to know if this is "normal" behavior -- i.e., is this a problem at all?
does the TCP/IP stack on Alphas always generate unaligned accesses? is
it a driver problem?

It doesn't seem to be hurting performance, but I guess I assumed that
the Linux kernel and (most) distributions and applications were 64-bit
clean.

Thanks,
Tom


