Why 2.2.19?  Is there something about the as1200 that isn't well
supported in the 2.4.x kernels?  I had many problems with my
up2000+ systems with dual cpu.  I would get many spinlocks.  They
aren't necessarily always bad, but the nodes would hang because of
them eventually.  I tried the 2.4.X series (currently 2.4.14) and
I very happy with the results.

Are you watching the node from the console or through the serial port?
If you are looking through the serial port, did you remember to build
"Character Devices/Support for console on Serial Port" for your new
kernel?

I see output like yours when the kernel kicks in but does not redirect
the output.  If the kernel is getting hung up for some reason (like
a manual fsck is needed) you aren't going to see it here.

Craig



