A couple of reasons.  First I personally prefer the redhat alpha 6.2
distro for older(pre-EV6) platforms.  Secondly I specifically needed a
2.2.x kernel for what I need to do with this box.  Simply put I often
start with 6.2 and build from there depending on what the system will be
used for.

6.2 is an excellent starting point for production quality systems i.e.:
mail servers, firewalls, etc.(in my opinion anyway)

Lastly I have had 2.2.19 running on alphas in production environments with
Zero downtime since 2.2.19 was released.

I am using the serial console and made all the needed changes that
requires.  I used a graphic head for the install but switched to serial as
soon as I had modified the inittab.  It ran perfectly for almost a week
before this happened.


