I'm looking to run a diskless system with the nfsroot coming from a separate 
Network Appliance server.  All of the dhcpd.conf examples I've seen show only 
how to use an nfs-root that's on the same system as the dhcp server.  Does 
anyone have an idea on how to get around this?  I've found that the following 
works on the system itself:

>>>b eib0 -fl '' -fl 'root=/dev/nfs console=ttyS0,19200 ip=dhcp 
nfsroot=<IP-ADDRESS OF SERVER>:<REMOTE FILESYSTEM>'

but, I was hoping someone might know of a way to do this through dhcp.

Thanks...




