On Tue, 18 Dec 2001, Divya Rehan wrote:

> Hi,
> 
> I am trying to install RH 7.0 (tried 7.1 aswell), but keep getting stuck at
> a particular Milo screen.  I have tried using Milo 2.2.17 and 18 with the
> same result.  I can load the older 2.0.x version of MILO but I do believe
> that the newer one is needed for RH 7/7.1 because of the different kernel.
> 
> Milo seems to hang on the "Swapping to PALcode at 0x8000 ..." line.

Well, you could use the old MILO but you'll need to build the boot
floppy. The install is now dependant on initrd images and the newer MILOs
can load these, the older can not. However if you build the root floppy
you should be able to around that. Then instead of passing the kernel the
CD as the root fs pass it the floppy...something like:

root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1
 
> The computer is an Alpha XL 366, I am using the XLT milo image, and the
> AlphaBios version is 5.70.

Have you tried the Alcor image instead of the XLT image?
 
> Any help would be greatly appreciated,
> Thanks.

--rdp

