You could solder them to the original slotB, but you wont gain any speed
advantage cuz...
1. Unsupported clock mult... 667 works and 833 works (on a UP2000+)
2. You'd need an SROM that supported it... which doesn't exist
3. The chipset needs to support that CPU speed, which it doesnt

fastest you could run the thing safely is 667MHz which you already have.


Kurt



