It asks you the questions again?  None of the commands I posted
configure the kernel. they only build it from the answer file's created
by (config, menuconfig or xconfig).. did you "SAVE and exit from
xconfig?  are you logged in as root or a superuser(su)

dep - builds the compiler and linker commands for all the modules
required for the build
clean - removes the intermediate files left from previous builds,
forcing a total rebuild.
boot - compiles and links the kernel image.
modules - builds the *.o files to be installed in the modules library.
modules_install - moves the modules created (*.o) into
/lib/modules/(kernel-version)/* 

Which kernel version are you trying to build.

A hint.. edit the Makefile  than add a identifier to the symbol
EXTRAVERSION=
as   EXTRAVERSION=TB

Then you can keep your kernels separate, by changing it   (TB1, TB2 etc.
) as you build your versions.


JJ



