I'm running linux on a dual-cpu (666MHz EV67) DS20E with 2G ram.  I've 
recently made the just to the 2.4.9-12 (with redhat 7.1) kernel and seen some 
problems with memory not being de-allocated.  For example, if I start with a 
freshly rebooted machine, I'll have 1.9G listed as MemFree (in /proc/meminfo).

# cat /proc/meminfo 
        total:    used:    free:  shared: buffers:  cached:
Mem:  2104926208 71933952 2032992256        0   892928 27287552
Swap: 2622472192        0 2622472192
