On Sun, Dec 30, 2001 at 11:34:13AM -0800, Brian Kurotsuchi wrote:
> 
> The IDE disk is partitioned BSD-style; I did it using fdisk and fdisk
> recognizes this at startup when I point it at that disk.  I e2writeboot-ed it
> using the instructions at alphalinux.org.

Are you sure?  'e2writeboot' will write a boot block but on a floppy.
To do that on a hard disk you are using 'swriteboot'.  There is also
'isomarkboot' for CDs.  Yes, utility names are "historic" and somewhat
confusing.

It would be nice to see an output of 'fdisk -l ...' for a disk on
which you attempt to put that boot block.  This may tell more why
you are having troubles.

  Michal




